      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alcan_Border%2C_Alaska"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name comes from the Alcan–Beaver Creek Border Crossing, the main U.S. port of entry for road travelers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alcan_Border%2C_Alaska"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Alcan Border’s residents work mainly for federal customs at the border crossing, forming the community’s core workforce.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alcan_Border%2C_Alaska"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A single central generator powers the whole community, with electricity supplied by Alaska Power & Telephone.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alcan_Border%2C_Alaska"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The area experiences a dry‑winter continental subarctic climate, with long, cold winters and short summers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alcan_Border%2C_Alaska"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Because Alcan Border lies in the Unorganized Borough, it has no local tax authority and no state‑operated schools.",
